w23-termination-lag
-------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code, data,
traces, patches or weights.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
Musa Cim, Burak Topcu and Mahmut Taylan Kandemir.
"Termination Lag: Coding Agents Solve Early but Stop Late".
arXiv:2611.14960, v1, submitted 11 Nov 2026 (2026-11-11 12:11:00 KST).
Primary category cs.AI, cross-listed cs.CL.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.14960
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ (a paper licence, not a
software grant).

Code: the abs page links no code repository. None was found or used.

Method only: the idea of recording every patch an agent produces during a
run, testing each one, marking the first correct patch, measuring
termination lag as the number of steps from that patch to the end of the
run, and noting that continued activity can undo an earlier correct patch.
The step gate that refuses a later breaking edit, the rule that protection
never expires, the stop-at-first-pass arm, the final-state baseline, the
fixture checks, the oracle and the fixtures are this sketch's own rules,
not the paper's. No text, figures, tables or data from the paper are copied
into the code; the PDF was not read; no agent, model or benchmark was run.
The paper's claims appear only in paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked
UNVERIFIED.
